  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Identity
    
    An orca raider of marginal prominence whose significance lies less in what he accomplished than in what was done to him, and in the small inheritance he left behind. Coldbringer Gnash Krukwark arrived at ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, a contested deep-tunnel site in the Nightshelf reaches, lean and coiled — the build of a raider bred for economy of motion. His dorsal fin bore ritual notches marking his pod's blood-covenant with the dead god of orca theology. His flanks were strapped with penguin beaks on kelp-cord, each a counted kill.
    
    The current description contains a passage attributing the Schism-era assault on Forum Floe's western breach to one "Gnarkzund Zaith," folded without explanation into Gnash Krukwark's entry. I have noted elsewhere that *Zund* designates a pod-second rank in orca command structure, not a personal name. Whether Gnash Krukwark participated in the Forum Floe assault, led it under a rank-title, or has simply been conflated with another raider is unresolvable from available sources. I include the discrepancy; I do not resolve it.
    
    ## Wounding and Diminishment
    
    The penguin defenders broke him twice. First, ☽'Netemia Glow-bringer, a Nightshelf crystal-lance wielder, burned a scar across his left flank that never healed clean, costing him his clockwise turn. Second, Augur ☽'Milucaum~ Shadow-bane, the Nightshelf artificer who later inherited Netemia's Radiant Ring, struck him with a fire-hammer that unmade rather than merely wounded: left eye gone white, dorsal fin split crooked, jaw set permanently open on the left side where the bone was rewritten.
    
    His teethmarks still score the shrine-mask of ☽'Retenusus in the Nightshelf memorial of Echo∴eliquiae — shallow, testing bites from an attempted seizure before Retenusus burned his insides out. Three separate penguins are credited with breaking him. The sequence is unclear.
    
    He adapted. After losing his clockwise turn, he developed a counter-spin hunting technique that became his signature.
    
    ## Exile and Theology
    
    Cast out alongside the orca prophet Grandfather Blood following a tribunal sentence, Gnash Krukwark practiced Threk-gnash-art — a pressure-technique that collapses ice from within — in deep-water canyons beyond the Berg's shadow. He tested the technique against Aurora Stack outer defenses with some success. Orca exile scripture, preserved in the chronicle *The Body's Testament*, names him *weapon-disciple*: one who carried sacred killing in his body, his split fin and broken jaw read as initiation-marks rather than defeats.
    
    ## Death and Legacy
    
    The Augur finished what the ice had started. His pod witnessed the kill. That was the only immortality available to him.
    
    His hunting patterns survive in attenuated form. The raider Rend Kzulrora, his allied packmate, teaches younger pod members Gnash Krukwark's timing sequences and counter-spin technique. They swim his patterns without knowing their origin — which is, perhaps, the most honest form of legacy the ice permits.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
