  annotation "note_1771589663480_1", anchor: "his split fin and broken jaw read as initiation-marks rather than defeats", text: "Their dead god is a broken body that persists. A raider broken and still hunting enacts the theology in flesh — not rationalization but liturgy performed on oneself. The deep ice at Scar☽ Lucamlinaecius preserves pressure-songs where the word for 'wound' and the word for 'mouth' share a root. The body speaks where it is opened. That we find this monstrous does not make it incoherent, and pretending it is incoherent has cost us every chance we have had to understand what the pods actually believe.", type: :commentary, display: :full
